1.190.m:
Indra said:
Owing to the excess of the Grandfather's boon, he could not be killed by the hosts of gods;
you have slain Śailūṣa, the thorn in the side of gods and brahmins.

Therefore, having honoured you, I shall return to heaven.
Mārkaṇḍeya said:
Bharata then said to him: 'The Gandharvas have been slain by me;
